<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
  <p class="font-bold">The ant walks, but the part of the rope under it stretches too.</p>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 300 182"
    class="w-full max-w-sm"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="ant-rope-title ant-rope-desc"
  >
    <title id="ant-rope-title">Three stages of a rope growing as an ant progresses</title>
    <desc id="ant-rope-desc">
      A rope expands in length; a marked ant is carried along as the entire rope stretches.
      Walking adds to its fraction of the rope crossed.
    </desc>
    <g fill="none" stroke="#387a91" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round">
      <path d="M16 34 H99" />
      <path d="M16 88 H168" />
      <path d="M16 166 H286" />
    </g>
    <g fill="#bd4b37" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1">
      <circle cx="37" cy="34" r="8" />
      <circle cx="68" cy="88" r="8" />
      <circle cx="144" cy="166" r="8" />
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="16">
      <text x="10" y="16">
        Earlier
      </text>
      <text x="10" y="70">
        Later
      </text>
      <text x="10" y="148">
        Later still
      </text>
      <text x="116" y="40">
        Rope stretches
      </text>
      <text x="10" y="114">
        The ant moves too
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">
    The drawings are schematic snapshots, not measured positions. The rope behind the ant grows
    and carries it along. Each small walk adds a fraction of the rope’s length; those fractions
    accumulate until it reaches the far end, even though the rope grows faster than the ant
    walks.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
